From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: 新增 HX83121A 级联从片（主动笔）驱动

MateBook E Go 屏幕的触摸控制器是一对 HX83121A：himax-spi 驱动的是 spi6 上的
主片（手指）；感应 M-Pencil 的是 spi20 上的级联从片（ACPI THPB/HIMX0002），
之前没有驱动。笔的位置、悬停和倾斜都要从从片取得，在主片的 raw 网格上做
判断分不开"极近悬停"与"真接触"（见 #21、#22 的讨论）。

本驱动只碰从片，不影响手指触摸：
- 检查总线、读芯片 ID，做 Windows THP 抓包中看到的两次写入
  （raw_out_sel = 0xF6、rawdata 地址 = 0x5AA5），之后从片开始出帧；
- 按 GPIO 39 中断读取 339 字节的帧（TX1/TX2 两组锚点与 9×9 网格），内容有
  变化的帧经 /dev/gk3_pen 交给用户态（read / poll，每次一个 struct pen_rec），
  由 gk3pend 解算成触控笔；debugfs（gk3_pen/）保留计数和最近 1024 帧；
- 从片没有复位线，每次主片复位（熄屏亮屏、himax-spi 自恢复）都会把它带掉：
  帧头错乱或连续读失败时重新初始化，并用跟随面板的 1 秒看门狗在亮屏而无帧
  时重新初始化；开机时主片固件可能还在加载，首次初始化失败时由看门狗启动
  中断。熄屏时看门狗和下面的空闲轮询都靠面板的跟随回调停下，所以面板还没
  注册时 probe 返回 -EPROBE_DEFER；
- 省电：没有笔时从片每秒仍中断约 125 次，超过 idle_after_ms（默认 10 s）
  未见笔就关掉中断、每 idle_poll_ms（默认 50 ms）读一帧，见到笔立即恢复；
  用户态在笔 MCU 有报文时写一下 /dev/gk3_pen，提前唤醒；
- 把笔的电量注册为 power supply "m-pencil"（作用域为设备），由用户态写入
  电量与充电状态。它不挂父设备：Android 为输入设备找电池时，从设备节点往上
  找最近的 power_supply 目录，uinput 笔位于 /sys/devices/virtual，因此会被
  认作触控笔的电池。它不建唤醒源：笔的电量不需要唤醒系统，而唤醒源会在它
  下面建 wakeup/ 目录并沿用它的 SELinux 标签，system_suspend 读取时被拒绝；
- 设备状态带引用计数：probe 持有一个，/dev/gk3_pen 每个打开的文件各持有一个，
  读写和 poll 都经由文件找到它。上一级 SPI 控制器被解绑时，remove 只标记设备
  已移除、唤醒等待者，状态等最后一个文件关闭才释放；驱动本身不提供 sysfs 的
  bind / unbind（suppress_bind_attrs）。

依赖写成 DRM || !DRM（与 i2c-hid 相同）：面板跟随的接口编在 DRM 核心模块里，
DRM=m 时本驱动只能编成模块。

笔 MCU（USB 12d1:10b8）在系统休眠恢复后不再转发压感，只有 USB 端口复位能
恢复，需要 usbcore.quirks=12d1:10b8:b，由启动参数提供，不在本驱动里处理。

实测：同一份代码以树外模块的形式在 1.0.0-rc.1 上使用（KernelSU 模块，
见 #26），树内版本只去掉了运行时 DT overlay（改由设备树提供节点）和 USB
怪癖的处理；已在本仓基线上编译通过，W=1 无警告，checkpatch 无错误、无警告。
不建唤醒源、等待面板和 suppress_bind_attrs 这三处也先在模块上验证过：
m-pencil 下不再有 wakeup 目录，system_suspend 不再被拒绝，驱动目录里没有
bind / unbind，熄屏时空闲轮询停止，笔的各项功能照常。等待面板的那条路径在
模块上走不到（加载时面板早已注册）。在 gk3pend 开着 /dev/gk3_pen 时解绑、再
重新绑定上一级 SPI 控制器（890000.spi）：解绑时驱动安全移除，gk3pend 收到
POLLHUP 后正常退出，内核没有报错；重新绑定后驱动重新初始化，gk3pend 被服务
重新拉起，笔照常可用。
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/Kconfig              |   17 +
 drivers/input/touchscreen/Makefile             |    1 +
 drivers/input/touchscreen/himax_hx83121a_pen.c | 1168 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 1186 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/input/touchscreen/himax_hx83121a_pen.c

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/Kconfig b/drivers/input/touchscreen/Kconfig
index 0aa769562..263376618 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/Kconfig
@@ -1430,4 +1430,21 @@ config TOUCHSCREEN_HIMAX_HX83121A_SPI
 
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
 	  module will be called himax_hx83121a_spi.
+
+config TOUCHSCREEN_HIMAX_HX83121A_PEN
+	tristate "Himax HX83121A cascade slave (active pen)"
+	depends on SPI && POWER_SUPPLY
+	depends on DRM || !DRM
+	help
+	  Say Y here to enable the pen-sensing cascade slave of the Himax
+	  HX83121A touch controller in the HUAWEI MateBook E Go (gaokun3).
+	  The driver hands the raw pen frames to userspace through
+	  /dev/gk3_pen, where gk3pend turns them into a stylus, and
+	  registers the pen's battery as a power supply.
+
+	  If unsure, say N.
+
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
+	  module will be called himax_hx83121a_pen.
+
 endif
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/Makefile b/drivers/input/touchscreen/Makefile
index 329afd486..5c3d544ec 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/Makefile
@@ -121,3 +121,4 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_ZINITIX)	+= zinitix.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_HIMAX_HX83112B)	+= himax_hx83112b.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_HIMAX_HX83121A_SPI)	+= himax_hx83121a_spi.o
 himax_hx83121a_spi-y			:= himax-spi-core.o hx-algo.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_HIMAX_HX83121A_PEN)	+= himax_hx83121a_pen.o
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax_hx83121a_pen.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax_hx83121a_pen.c
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..f7f513c8c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax_hx83121a_pen.c
@@ -0,0 +1,1168 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+/*
+ * Himax HX83121A cascade slave (active pen) on the HUAWEI MateBook E Go
+ * (gaokun3).
+ *
+ * The panel's touch controller is a pair of HX83121A.  himax-spi drives the
+ * master on spi6 (finger touch); the slave, which senses the M-Pencil, is a
+ * separate SPI device on spi20 (ACPI THPB/HIMX0002).  This driver:
+ *
+ *   1. binds to the slave (the gaokun3 DT enables spi20 and its pins and
+ *      describes the slave), checks the bus and reads the IC ID;
+ *   2. does the two slave writes seen in the Windows THP capture
+ *      (raw_out_sel = 0xF6, rawdata address = 0x5AA5);
+ *   3. reads the 339-byte slave frame (3-byte command + 4-byte IC header +
+ *      TX1/TX2 blocks of anchor row/col + 9x9 s16 grid) by polling, or on the
+ *      GPIO 39 interrupt with use_irq=1;
+ *   4. keeps counters and the last 1024 frames in debugfs (gk3_pen/);
+ *   5. hands every frame whose content changed to userspace through
+ *      /dev/gk3_pen (blocking read / poll, one struct pen_rec per read);
+ *   6. re-initialises the slave when the header stops reading 5a a5 or reads
+ *      keep failing, and, from a 1 s watchdog that follows the panel, when no
+ *      frame arrived for a second while the screen is on.  The slave has no
+ *      reset line: every master reset (screen off/on, himax-spi recovery)
+ *      takes it down too, and an unconfigured slave raises no interrupts at
+ *      all, so in use_irq mode only the watchdog can notice.  The interrupt
+ *      is only requested once an init succeeded (an unconfigured slave could
+ *      hold the level-low line); at boot the driver can probe while himax-spi
+ *      is still reloading the master's firmware, so the first init may fail
+ *      and the watchdog's first good re-init starts the interrupt;
+ *   7. saves wakeups while no pen is around: the slave interrupts ~125 times
+ *      a second even without a pen, so after idle_after_ms with no TX1
+ *      anchor the interrupt is switched off and one frame is read every
+ *      idle_poll_ms instead; the first frame with an anchor switches the
+ *      interrupt back on.  Unread frames are simply overwritten by the
+ *      slave, as with slow polling, and the master keeps running.  Polling
+ *      alone notices a pen too late for a quick tap, so userspace also
+ *      writes to /dev/gk3_pen whenever the pen controller reports activity
+ *      (its reports start as soon as the pen is picked up, before it is
+ *      anywhere near the screen): that switches the interrupt back on at
+ *      once and keeps the slave awake while the pen is in use;
+ *   8. registers the pen's battery as power supply "m-pencil" (scope device,
+ *      so healthd leaves it out of the system battery).  The pen controller
+ *      reports the level (event 0x08, percent) and charging (0x09) to
+ *      userspace, which passes them on with a 3-byte write to /dev/gk3_pen.
+ *      It has no parent device on purpose: Android's EventHub looks for
+ *      batteries in the nearest power_supply directory above an input
+ *      device's sysfs node, which for gk3pend's uinput pen is
+ *      /sys/devices/virtual, so the battery shows up as the stylus's
+ *      (settings, low-battery notice).  The core warns about the missing
+ *      parent once at registration.
+ *
+ * Userspace (gk3pend) turns the frames into a stylus: position, hover and
+ * tilt from the frames, pressure, side double-tap and battery from the pen
+ * controller on USB (12d1:10b8).  That controller holds its reports across
+ * a system suspend until the host talks to it on each interface: usbhid
+ * does it for pressure (HID_QUIRK_IDLE_ON_RESUME), gk3pend for the side
+ * double-tap.  Without it the pen still shows as connected but pressure
+ * stays off.
+ *
+ * It never touches the master, so finger touch is unaffected.
+ *
+ * Bus protocol: same as himax-spi-core.c (himax_spi_read/write,
+ * himax_mcu_register_read/write, himax_mcu_interface_on) with the slave's
+ * function codes F5 (read) / F4 (write) instead of the master's F3 / F2.
+ */
+#define pr_fmt(fmt) KBUILD_MODNAME ": " fmt
+
+#include <linux/debugfs.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <linux/freezer.h>
+#include <linux/interrupt.h>
+#include <linux/kref.h>
+#include <linux/kthread.h>
+#include <linux/ktime.h>
+#include <linux/miscdevice.h>
+#include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/mutex.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
+#include <linux/poll.h>
+#include <linux/power_supply.h>
+#include <linux/seq_file.h>
+#include <linux/slab.h>
+#include <linux/spi/spi.h>
+#include <linux/uaccess.h>
+#include <linux/unaligned.h>
+#include <linux/vmalloc.h>
+#include <linux/wait.h>
+#include <linux/workqueue.h>
+
+#include <drm/drm_panel.h>
+
+static int spi_mode = 3;
+module_param(spi_mode, int, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(spi_mode, "SPI mode 0..3 (master runs mode 3; ACPI says 0)");
+
+static int speed_hz = 12000000;
+module_param(speed_hz, int, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(speed_hz, "SPI clock");
+
+static int poll_hz = 120;
+module_param(poll_hz, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(poll_hz, "frame polling rate when use_irq=0");
+
+static bool use_irq = true;
+module_param(use_irq, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(use_irq, "read frames on the GPIO 39 interrupt (default); 0 = poll at poll_hz");
+
+static bool irq_edge;
+module_param(irq_edge, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(irq_edge, "trigger on the falling edge instead of the DT's level-low");
+
+static bool do_init = true;
+module_param(do_init, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(do_init, "write raw_out_sel/rawdata_addr after the bus check");
+
+static int idle_after_ms = 10000;	/* longer than a pause while drawing */
+module_param(idle_after_ms, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(idle_after_ms, "use_irq: switch the interrupt off after this long without a pen and poll instead (0 = never)");
+
+static int idle_poll_ms = 50;
+module_param(idle_poll_ms, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(idle_poll_ms, "frame polling period while idle");
+
+#define F_READ			0xf5
+#define F_WRITE			0xf4
+
+#define AHB_ADDR_BYTE_0		0x00
+#define AHB_RDATA_BYTE_0	0x08
+#define AHB_ACCESS_DIRECTION	0x0c
+#define AHB_INCR4		0x0d
+#define AHB_CONTI		0x13
+#define AHB_EVENT_STACK		0x30
+
+#define AHB_CMD_CONTI		0x31
+#define AHB_CMD_INCR4		0x10
+#define AHB_CMD_INCR4_ADD_4	0x01
+#define AHB_CMD_DIR_READ	0x00
+
+#define REG_ICID		0x900000d0
+#define REG_RAW_OUT_SEL		0x100072ec	/* EGoTouchRev pfw_op.addr_raw_out_sel */
+#define REG_RAWDATA_ADDR	0x10000000	/* EGoTouchRev psram_op.addr_rawdata_addr */
+
+#define HDR_LEN			3		/* function, command, dummy */
+#define FRAME_LEN		336		/* 4-byte IC header + 166 words */
+#define WORDS_OFF		4
+#define TX2_WORD		83		/* TX1 block = words 0..82 */
+#define GRID			81
+
+#define RING_LEN		1024
+
+/* Header of a slave frame once raw_out_sel/rawdata_addr are in effect. */
+#define HDR_OK(d)		((d)[0] == 0x5a && (d)[1] == 0xa5)
+#define REINIT_AFTER		30		/* bad frames in a row (~250 ms) */
+
+/* Also the record handed out by read() on /dev/gk3_pen. */
+struct pen_rec {
+	u64 t_ns;
+	u32 seq;
+	u32 flags;			/* bit0: TX1 anchor valid */
+	u8 data[FRAME_LEN];
+};
+
+struct gk3_pen {
+	struct kref ref;		/* probe, plus one per open /dev/gk3_pen */
+	struct spi_device *spi;
+	struct mutex lock;		/* SPI access and stats */
+	u8 *xfer;			/* HDR_LEN + FRAME_LEN, kmalloc'd for DMA */
+	struct task_struct *poller;
+	struct dentry *dbg;
+	bool running;
+
+	u8 bus_conti, bus_incr4;
+	u32 icid, raw_out_sel;
+	int bus_ret, init_ret;
+
+	u32 seq, frames, errors, dups, zeros, irqs, hdr_bad;
+	u32 tx1_valid, tx2_valid;
+	u16 tx1_row, tx1_col, tx2_row, tx2_col;
+	s16 tx1_peak, tx1_peak_max, tx2_peak;
+	u8 last[FRAME_LEN];
+	struct pen_rec *ring;
+	u32 ring_head;
+
+	/* newest frame whose content changed, for /dev/gk3_pen */
+	struct pen_rec uniq;
+	u32 uniq_seq;
+	wait_queue_head_t wq;
+	struct miscdevice misc;
+	bool misc_ok, gone;
+
+	u32 bad_frames, reinits;
+	unsigned long last_reinit;
+
+	/* screen state from the panel, and the stall watchdog */
+	struct drm_panel_follower follower;
+	bool follower_ok, panel_on;
+	struct delayed_work watchdog;
+	u32 wd_frames, wd_reinits;
+
+	/* idle: no pen for idle_after_ms, interrupt off, poll every idle_poll_ms */
+	bool idle;
+	unsigned long pen_seen;		/* jiffies of the last frame with a TX1 anchor */
+	u32 pen_frames;			/* complete frames with a TX1 anchor */
+	struct delayed_work idle_poll;
+	u32 idle_enters, idle_polls;
+	u32 hints, hint_wakes;		/* pen-in-use writes, and those that ended idle */
+};
+
+/*
+ * There is one slave; opening the char device finds it here.  Each open
+ * file holds a reference, so the state outlives an unbind (of the parent
+ * SPI controller, say) while gk3pend still has /dev/gk3_pen open.
+ */
+static struct gk3_pen *gk3_pen_dev;
+static DEFINE_MUTEX(gk3_pen_dev_lock);
+
+static void pen_free(struct kref *ref)
+{
+	kfree(container_of(ref, struct gk3_pen, ref));
+}
+
+static void pen_put(void *data)
+{
+	struct gk3_pen *p = data;
+
+	kref_put(&p->ref, pen_free);
+}
+
+/* ---- bus primitives (himax-spi-core.c with F5/F4) ---- */
+
+static int pen_read(struct gk3_pen *p, u8 cmd, u8 *out, u32 len)
+{
+	struct spi_transfer x = {
+		.tx_buf = p->xfer,
+		.rx_buf = p->xfer,
+		.len = HDR_LEN + len,
+	};
+	int ret;
+
+	memset(p->xfer, 0, HDR_LEN + len);
+	p->xfer[0] = F_READ;
+	p->xfer[1] = cmd;
+	ret = spi_sync_transfer(p->spi, &x, 1);
+	if (!ret)
+		memcpy(out, p->xfer + HDR_LEN, len);
+	return ret;
+}
+
+static int pen_write(struct gk3_pen *p, u8 cmd, const u8 *addr, const u8 *data, u32 len)
+{
+	struct spi_transfer x = { .tx_buf = p->xfer };
+	u32 n = 2;
+
+	p->xfer[0] = F_WRITE;
+	p->xfer[1] = cmd;
+	if (addr) {
+		memcpy(p->xfer + n, addr, 4);
+		n += 4;
+	}
+	if (data && len) {
+		memcpy(p->xfer + n, data, len);
+		n += len;
+	}
+	x.len = n;
+	return spi_sync_transfer(p->spi, &x, 1);
+}
+
+static int pen_burst(struct gk3_pen *p, bool add4)
+{
+	u8 v = AHB_CMD_CONTI;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = pen_write(p, AHB_CONTI, NULL, &v, 1);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	v = AHB_CMD_INCR4 | (add4 ? AHB_CMD_INCR4_ADD_4 : 0);
+	return pen_write(p, AHB_INCR4, NULL, &v, 1);
+}
+
+static int pen_reg_read(struct gk3_pen *p, u32 addr, u8 *out, u32 len)
+{
+	u8 a[4], dir = AHB_CMD_DIR_READ;
+	int ret;
+
+	put_unaligned_le32(addr, a);
+	ret = pen_burst(p, len > 4);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	ret = pen_write(p, AHB_ADDR_BYTE_0, a, NULL, 0);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	ret = pen_write(p, AHB_ACCESS_DIRECTION, NULL, &dir, 1);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	ret = pen_read(p, AHB_RDATA_BYTE_0, out, len);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	return pen_burst(p, !(len > 4));
+}
+
+static int pen_reg_write(struct gk3_pen *p, u32 addr, const u8 *data, u32 len)
+{
+	u8 a[4];
+	int ret;
+
+	put_unaligned_le32(addr, a);
+	ret = pen_burst(p, len > 4);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	ret = pen_write(p, AHB_ADDR_BYTE_0, a, data, len);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	return pen_burst(p, !(len > 4));
+}
+
+/* himax_mcu_interface_on(): wake the bus, set burst mode, read it back. */
+static int pen_bus_check(struct gk3_pen *p)
+{
+	u8 dummy[4];
+	int i, ret;
+
+	ret = pen_read(p, AHB_RDATA_BYTE_0, dummy, 4);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	for (i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
+		ret = pen_burst(p, false);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+		ret = pen_read(p, AHB_CONTI, &p->bus_conti, 1);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+		ret = pen_read(p, AHB_INCR4, &p->bus_incr4, 1);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+		if (p->bus_conti == AHB_CMD_CONTI && p->bus_incr4 == AHB_CMD_INCR4)
+			return 0;
+		usleep_range(1000, 1100);
+	}
+	return -EIO;
+}
+
+#define PLOG(v, dev, fmt, ...)					\
+	do {							\
+		if (v)						\
+			dev_info(dev, fmt, ##__VA_ARGS__);	\
+		else						\
+			dev_dbg(dev, fmt, ##__VA_ARGS__);	\
+	} while (0)
+
+static int pen_hw_init(struct gk3_pen *p, bool verbose)
+{
+	struct device *dev = &p->spi->dev;
+	static const u8 raw_sel[4] = { 0xf6, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00 };
+	static const u8 raw_addr[4] = { 0xa5, 0x5a, 0x00, 0x00 };
+	u8 v[4];
+	int i, ret;
+
+	p->bus_ret = pen_bus_check(p);
+	PLOG(verbose, dev, "bus check %d: conti=0x%02x (want 0x31) incr4=0x%02x (want 0x10)\n",
+	     p->bus_ret, p->bus_conti, p->bus_incr4);
+	if (p->bus_ret)
+		return p->bus_ret;
+
+	ret = pen_reg_read(p, REG_ICID, v, 4);
+	p->icid = ret ? 0 : get_unaligned_le32(v);
+	PLOG(verbose, dev, "ICID read %d: 0x%08x (master reads 0x83121a00-ish)\n", ret, p->icid);
+
+	if (!do_init)
+		return 0;
+
+	/* EGoTouchRev himax_switch_data_type(Slave, EGO_RAWDATA): write + verify */
+	ret = -EIO;
+	for (i = 0; i < 50; i++) {
+		if (pen_reg_write(p, REG_RAW_OUT_SEL, raw_sel, 4) == 0 &&
+		    pen_reg_read(p, REG_RAW_OUT_SEL, v, 4) == 0) {
+			p->raw_out_sel = get_unaligned_le32(v);
+			if (v[0] == raw_sel[0]) {
+				ret = 0;
+				break;
+			}
+		}
+		usleep_range(1000, 1100);
+	}
+	PLOG(verbose, dev, "raw_out_sel <- 0xf6: %d after %d tries (read back 0x%08x)\n",
+	     ret, i + 1, p->raw_out_sel);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/* EGoTouchRev register_write(slave, addr_rawdata_addr, A5 5A 00 00) */
+	ret = pen_reg_write(p, REG_RAWDATA_ADDR, raw_addr, 4);
+	PLOG(verbose, dev, "rawdata_addr <- 0x5aa5: %d\n", ret);
+	return ret;
+}
+
+/* ---- frames ---- */
+
+static s16 grid_peak(const u8 *w, int first_word)
+{
+	s16 peak = S16_MIN;
+	int i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < GRID; i++) {
+		s16 v = (s16)get_unaligned_le16(w + 2 * (first_word + i));
+
+		if (v > peak)
+			peak = v;
+	}
+	return peak;
+}
+
+static void pen_account(struct gk3_pen *p, const u8 *d, ktime_t t)
+{
+	const u8 *w = d + WORDS_OFF;
+	struct pen_rec *r = &p->ring[p->ring_head];
+	bool valid1, valid2, zero = !memchr_inv(d, 0, FRAME_LEN);
+
+	p->tx1_row = get_unaligned_le16(w);
+	p->tx1_col = get_unaligned_le16(w + 2);
+	p->tx2_row = get_unaligned_le16(w + 2 * TX2_WORD);
+	p->tx2_col = get_unaligned_le16(w + 2 * TX2_WORD + 2);
+	valid1 = !((p->tx1_row & 0xff) == 0xff && (p->tx1_col & 0xff) == 0xff);
+	valid2 = !((p->tx2_row & 0xff) == 0xff && (p->tx2_col & 0xff) == 0xff);
+	p->tx1_peak = grid_peak(w, 2);
+	p->tx2_peak = grid_peak(w, TX2_WORD + 2);
+
+	p->frames++;
+	if (zero)
+		p->zeros++;
+	/*
+	 * Only complete frames go to userspace.  With the pen in range the
+	 * slave runs at ~240 Hz and a read seems to consume the frame: reading
+	 * again before the next one returns zeros, and a read that races the
+	 * update returns a torn buffer.  Both lack the 5a a5 header.
+	 */
+	if (!HDR_OK(d)) {
+		p->hdr_bad++;
+	} else if (!memcmp(d, p->last, FRAME_LEN)) {
+		p->dups++;
+	} else {
+		p->uniq.t_ns = ktime_to_ns(t);
+		p->uniq.seq = p->seq;
+		p->uniq.flags = valid1;
+		memcpy(p->uniq.data, d, FRAME_LEN);
+		WRITE_ONCE(p->uniq_seq, p->uniq_seq + 1);
+		wake_up_interruptible(&p->wq);
+	}
+	if (valid1) {
+		p->tx1_valid++;
+		if (p->tx1_peak > p->tx1_peak_max)
+			p->tx1_peak_max = p->tx1_peak;
+		if (HDR_OK(d)) {
+			p->pen_frames++;
+			p->pen_seen = jiffies;
+		}
+	}
+	if (valid2)
+		p->tx2_valid++;
+	if (HDR_OK(d))
+		memcpy(p->last, d, FRAME_LEN);
+
+	r->t_ns = ktime_to_ns(t);
+	r->seq = p->seq++;
+	r->flags = valid1;
+	memcpy(r->data, d, FRAME_LEN);
+	p->ring_head = (p->ring_head + 1) % RING_LEN;
+
+	if (p->frames <= 3)
+		dev_info(&p->spi->dev, "frame %u hdr %*ph tx1 %04x/%04x peak %d tx2 %04x/%04x\n",
+			 p->frames, 4, d, p->tx1_row, p->tx1_col, p->tx1_peak,
+			 p->tx2_row, p->tx2_col);
+}
+
+static void pen_read_and_account(struct gk3_pen *p)
+{
+	u8 frame[FRAME_LEN];
+	ktime_t t = ktime_get();
+	int ret;
+
+	mutex_lock(&p->lock);
+	ret = pen_read(p, AHB_EVENT_STACK, frame, FRAME_LEN);
+	if (ret)
+		p->errors++;
+	else
+		pen_account(p, frame, t);
+
+	/*
+	 * The slave has no reset line: every master reset (screen off/on,
+	 * himax-spi error recovery) takes it down too and drops our two
+	 * writes.  It then stops prefixing frames with 5a a5 (or stops
+	 * answering), so redo the init, at most once a second.
+	 */
+	if (ret || !HDR_OK(frame))
+		p->bad_frames++;
+	else
+		p->bad_frames = 0;
+	if (p->bad_frames >= REINIT_AFTER && time_after(jiffies, p->last_reinit + HZ)) {
+		p->last_reinit = jiffies;
+		p->reinits++;
+		p->init_ret = pen_hw_init(p, false);
+		dev_info(&p->spi->dev, "re-init #%u after %u bad frames: %d\n",
+			 p->reinits, p->bad_frames, p->init_ret);
+		if (!p->init_ret)
+			p->bad_frames = 0;
+	}
+	mutex_unlock(&p->lock);
+}
+
+static int pen_poll_fn(void *arg)
+{
+	struct gk3_pen *p = arg;
+
+	set_freezable();
+	while (!kthread_should_stop()) {
+		unsigned long period = 1000000UL / clamp(poll_hz, 1, 1000);
+
+		pen_read_and_account(p);
+		usleep_range(period > 200 ? period - 200 : period, period);
+		try_to_freeze();
+	}
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/* ---- idle: interrupt off and slow polling while no pen is in range ---- */
+
+static unsigned long idle_poll_period(void)
+{
+	return msecs_to_jiffies(max(READ_ONCE(idle_poll_ms), 1));
+}
+
+/* p->lock held; idle only ever starts from the interrupt thread */
+static void pen_set_idle(struct gk3_pen *p, bool idle)
+{
+	if (p->idle == idle)
+		return;
+	p->idle = idle;
+	if (idle) {
+		disable_irq_nosync(p->spi->irq);
+		p->idle_enters++;
+		queue_delayed_work(system_freezable_wq, &p->idle_poll, idle_poll_period());
+	} else {
+		enable_irq(p->spi->irq);
+	}
+}
+
+static void pen_idle_poll_fn(struct work_struct *work)
+{
+	struct gk3_pen *p = container_of(to_delayed_work(work), struct gk3_pen, idle_poll);
+	u32 seen;
+
+	mutex_lock(&p->lock);
+	seen = p->pen_frames;
+	mutex_unlock(&p->lock);
+	if (!READ_ONCE(p->idle))
+		return;
+
+	pen_read_and_account(p);
+
+	mutex_lock(&p->lock);
+	p->idle_polls++;
+	if (p->idle) {
+		if (p->pen_frames != seen)
+			pen_set_idle(p, false);
+		else
+			queue_delayed_work(system_freezable_wq, &p->idle_poll, idle_poll_period());
+	}
+	mutex_unlock(&p->lock);
+}
+
+static irqreturn_t pen_irq_fn(int irq, void *arg)
+{
+	struct gk3_pen *p = arg;
+	int after = READ_ONCE(idle_after_ms);
+
+	p->irqs++;
+	pen_read_and_account(p);
+
+	mutex_lock(&p->lock);
+	if (after > 0 && p->panel_on && !p->gone &&
+	    time_after(jiffies, p->pen_seen + msecs_to_jiffies(after)))
+		pen_set_idle(p, true);
+	mutex_unlock(&p->lock);
+	return IRQ_HANDLED;
+}
+
+static int pen_start(struct gk3_pen *p)
+{
+	unsigned long flags = IRQF_ONESHOT | (irq_edge ? IRQF_TRIGGER_FALLING : 0);
+	struct device *dev = &p->spi->dev;
+	int ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * Probe, the watchdog and debugfs reinit can all get here; the lock
+	 * keeps a second caller from starting the interrupt or the poller
+	 * twice.  A handler that fires right away waits for the lock.
+	 */
+	mutex_lock(&p->lock);
+	ret = 0;
+	if (p->running || p->gone)
+		goto out;
+	if (use_irq) {
+		if (p->spi->irq <= 0) {
+			ret = -ENXIO;
+			goto out;
+		}
+		p->pen_seen = jiffies;
+		ret = devm_request_threaded_irq(dev, p->spi->irq, NULL, pen_irq_fn,
+						flags, "himax-hx83121a-pen", p);
+		if (ret)
+			goto out;
+	} else {
+		p->poller = kthread_run(pen_poll_fn, p, "gk3-pen-poll");
+		if (IS_ERR(p->poller)) {
+			ret = PTR_ERR(p->poller);
+			p->poller = NULL;
+			goto out;
+		}
+	}
+	p->running = true;
+	dev_info(dev, "reading frames by %s\n", use_irq ? "interrupt" : "polling");
+out:
+	mutex_unlock(&p->lock);
+	return ret;
+}
+
+/* ---- stall watchdog + panel follower ---- */
+
+#define WD_PERIOD	msecs_to_jiffies(1000)
+
+/*
+ * With the screen on the slave delivers ~130 frames/s even without a pen, so a
+ * second without a single frame means it lost its configuration (a master
+ * reset took it down).  Re-init; if the master is still mid-reset this gets
+ * undone and the next tick tries again.
+ */
+static void pen_watchdog_fn(struct work_struct *work)
+{
+	struct gk3_pen *p = container_of(to_delayed_work(work), struct gk3_pen, watchdog);
+	bool start = false;
+	int ret;
+
+	if (!READ_ONCE(p->panel_on) || READ_ONCE(p->gone))
+		return;
+	mutex_lock(&p->lock);
+	if (p->frames == p->wd_frames) {
+		p->wd_reinits++;
+		p->init_ret = pen_hw_init(p, false);
+		dev_info(&p->spi->dev, "watchdog: no frame for 1 s, re-init #%u: %d\n",
+			 p->wd_reinits, p->init_ret);
+		/* probe skips the interrupt when its init failed (boot race) */
+		start = !p->init_ret && !p->running;
+	}
+	p->wd_frames = p->frames;
+	mutex_unlock(&p->lock);
+	if (start) {
+		ret = pen_start(p);
+		if (ret)
+			dev_err(&p->spi->dev, "start: %d\n", ret);
+	}
+	queue_delayed_work(system_freezable_wq, &p->watchdog, WD_PERIOD);
+}
+
+static int pen_panel_enabled(struct drm_panel_follower *f)
+{
+	struct gk3_pen *p = container_of(f, struct gk3_pen, follower);
+
+	mutex_lock(&p->lock);
+	p->pen_seen = jiffies;
+	mutex_unlock(&p->lock);
+	WRITE_ONCE(p->panel_on, true);
+	mod_delayed_work(system_freezable_wq, &p->watchdog, WD_PERIOD);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int pen_panel_disabling(struct drm_panel_follower *f)
+{
+	struct gk3_pen *p = container_of(f, struct gk3_pen, follower);
+
+	WRITE_ONCE(p->panel_on, false);
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&p->watchdog);
+	/* back to interrupt mode: with the screen off nothing arrives anyway */
+	mutex_lock(&p->lock);
+	pen_set_idle(p, false);
+	mutex_unlock(&p->lock);
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&p->idle_poll);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static const struct drm_panel_follower_funcs pen_follower_funcs = {
+	.panel_enabled = pen_panel_enabled,
+	.panel_disabling = pen_panel_disabling,
+};
+
+/* ---- debugfs ---- */
+
+static int stats_show(struct seq_file *s, void *unused)
+{
+	struct gk3_pen *p = s->private;
+
+	mutex_lock(&p->lock);
+	seq_printf(s, "spi_mode %d speed_hz %d use_irq %d poll_hz %d running %d irq %d\n",
+		   p->spi->mode & 3, p->spi->max_speed_hz, use_irq, poll_hz, p->running,
+		   p->spi->irq);
+	seq_printf(s, "bus_check %d conti 0x%02x incr4 0x%02x icid 0x%08x init %d raw_out_sel 0x%08x\n",
+		   p->bus_ret, p->bus_conti, p->bus_incr4, p->icid, p->init_ret, p->raw_out_sel);
+	seq_printf(s, "frames %u errors %u dups %u zeros %u irqs %u uniq %u hdr_bad %u bad_run %u reinits %u\n",
+		   p->frames, p->errors, p->dups, p->zeros, p->irqs, p->uniq_seq,
+		   p->hdr_bad, p->bad_frames, p->reinits);
+	seq_printf(s, "tx1_valid %u tx2_valid %u peak_max %d panel_on %d follower %d wd_reinits %u\n",
+		   p->tx1_valid, p->tx2_valid, p->tx1_peak_max, p->panel_on, p->follower_ok,
+		   p->wd_reinits);
+	seq_printf(s, "idle %d enters %u polls %u hints %u hint_wakes %u (idle_after_ms %d idle_poll_ms %d)\n",
+		   p->idle, p->idle_enters, p->idle_polls, p->hints, p->hint_wakes,
+		   idle_after_ms, idle_poll_ms);
+	seq_printf(s, "last hdr %*ph tx1 %04x/%04x peak %d tx2 %04x/%04x peak %d\n",
+		   4, p->last, p->tx1_row, p->tx1_col, p->tx1_peak,
+		   p->tx2_row, p->tx2_col, p->tx2_peak);
+	mutex_unlock(&p->lock);
+	return 0;
+}
+DEFINE_SHOW_ATTRIBUTE(stats);
+
+/* ring: snapshot at open, records oldest to newest */
+static int ring_open(struct inode *inode, struct file *f)
+{
+	struct gk3_pen *p = inode->i_private;
+	size_t rec = sizeof(struct pen_rec);
+	u8 *snap = vmalloc(RING_LEN * rec);
+	u32 i;
+
+	if (!snap)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+	mutex_lock(&p->lock);
+	for (i = 0; i < RING_LEN; i++)
+		memcpy(snap + i * rec, &p->ring[(p->ring_head + i) % RING_LEN], rec);
+	mutex_unlock(&p->lock);
+	f->private_data = snap;
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static ssize_t ring_read(struct file *f, char __user *buf, size_t n, loff_t *pos)
+{
+	return simple_read_from_buffer(buf, n, pos, f->private_data,
+				       RING_LEN * sizeof(struct pen_rec));
+}
+
+static int ring_release(struct inode *inode, struct file *f)
+{
+	vfree(f->private_data);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static const struct file_operations ring_fops = {
+	.owner = THIS_MODULE,
+	.open = ring_open,
+	.read = ring_read,
+	.release = ring_release,
+	.llseek = default_llseek,
+};
+
+static ssize_t reinit_write(struct file *f, const char __user *buf, size_t n, loff_t *pos)
+{
+	struct gk3_pen *p = f->private_data;
+	int ret;
+
+	mutex_lock(&p->lock);
+	ret = pen_hw_init(p, true);
+	p->init_ret = ret;
+	mutex_unlock(&p->lock);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = pen_start(p);
+	return ret ? ret : n;
+}
+
+static const struct file_operations reinit_fops = {
+	.owner = THIS_MODULE,
+	.open = simple_open,
+	.write = reinit_write,
+};
+
+/* ---- /dev/gk3_pen: one struct pen_rec per read, newest changed frame ---- */
+
+struct pen_file {
+	struct gk3_pen *p;		/* referenced while the file is open */
+	u32 last;			/* uniq_seq this reader has seen */
+};
+
+static int pen_cdev_open(struct inode *inode, struct file *f)
+{
+	struct pen_file *pf;
+	struct gk3_pen *p;
+
+	pf = kzalloc_obj(*pf, GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!pf)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+	mutex_lock(&gk3_pen_dev_lock);
+	p = gk3_pen_dev;
+	if (p)
+		kref_get(&p->ref);
+	mutex_unlock(&gk3_pen_dev_lock);
+	if (!p) {
+		kfree(pf);
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
+	pf->p = p;
+	pf->last = READ_ONCE(p->uniq_seq);
+	f->private_data = pf;
+	return stream_open(inode, f);
+}
+
+static int pen_cdev_release(struct inode *inode, struct file *f)
+{
+	struct pen_file *pf = f->private_data;
+
+	pen_put(pf->p);
+	kfree(pf);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static ssize_t pen_cdev_read(struct file *f, char __user *buf, size_t n, loff_t *pos)
+{
+	struct pen_file *pf = f->private_data;
+	struct gk3_pen *p = pf->p;
+	struct pen_rec rec;
+	int ret;
+
+	if (READ_ONCE(p->gone))
+		return -ENODEV;
+	if (n < sizeof(rec))
+		return -EINVAL;
+	if (READ_ONCE(p->uniq_seq) == pf->last) {
+		if (f->f_flags & O_NONBLOCK)
+			return -EAGAIN;
+		ret = wait_event_interruptible(p->wq,
+					       READ_ONCE(p->uniq_seq) != pf->last ||
+					       READ_ONCE(p->gone));
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+		if (READ_ONCE(p->gone))
+			return -ENODEV;
+	}
+	mutex_lock(&p->lock);
+	rec = p->uniq;
+	pf->last = p->uniq_seq;
+	mutex_unlock(&p->lock);
+	if (copy_to_user(buf, &rec, sizeof(rec)))
+		return -EFAULT;
+	return sizeof(rec);
+}
+
+/* ---- pen battery (see 8. above) ---- */
+
+static int pen_bat_capacity = -1;	/* percent; -1 = not reported yet */
+static int pen_bat_charging = -1;	/* 0/1; -1 = not reported yet */
+static struct power_supply *pen_bat;
+
+static const enum power_supply_property pen_bat_props[] = {
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_PRESENT,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CAPACITY,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_SCOPE,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_MODEL_NAME,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_MANUFACTURER,
+};
+
+static int pen_bat_get(struct power_supply *psy, enum power_supply_property psp,
+		       union power_supply_propval *val)
+{
+	int cap = READ_ONCE(pen_bat_capacity), chg = READ_ONCE(pen_bat_charging);
+
+	switch (psp) {
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS:
+		if (cap < 0 || chg < 0)
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_UNKNOWN;
+		else if (!chg)
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING;
+		else
+			val->intval = cap >= 100 ? POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL :
+				      POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
+		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_PRESENT:
+		val->intval = cap >= 0;
+		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CAPACITY:
+		if (cap < 0)
+			return -ENODATA;
+		val->intval = cap;
+		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_SCOPE:
+		val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_SCOPE_DEVICE;
+		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_MODEL_NAME:
+		val->strval = "M-Pencil";
+		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_MANUFACTURER:
+		val->strval = "HUAWEI";
+		break;
+	default:
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static const struct power_supply_desc pen_bat_desc = {
+	.name = "m-pencil",
+	.type = POWER_SUPPLY_TYPE_BATTERY,
+	.properties = pen_bat_props,
+	.num_properties = ARRAY_SIZE(pen_bat_props),
+	.get_property = pen_bat_get,
+};
+
+/*
+ * Nothing about the pen's battery needs to wake the system, and a wakeup
+ * source would put a wakeup/ directory under the supply that inherits its
+ * SELinux label, which system_suspend is then denied reading.
+ */
+static const struct power_supply_config pen_bat_cfg = {
+	.no_wakeup_source = true,
+};
+
+/* 'B', level (0-100), charging (0/1); 0xff leaves that field as it is */
+static void pen_bat_set(const u8 *m)
+{
+	int cap = m[1] <= 100 ? m[1] : READ_ONCE(pen_bat_capacity);
+	int chg = m[2] <= 1 ? m[2] : READ_ONCE(pen_bat_charging);
+
+	if (cap == READ_ONCE(pen_bat_capacity) && chg == READ_ONCE(pen_bat_charging))
+		return;
+	WRITE_ONCE(pen_bat_capacity, cap);
+	WRITE_ONCE(pen_bat_charging, chg);
+	if (pen_bat)
+		power_supply_changed(pen_bat);
+}
+
+/*
+ * A battery message (above), or any other write: the pen is in use (its
+ * controller is reporting), so stay awake.
+ */
+static ssize_t pen_cdev_write(struct file *f, const char __user *buf, size_t n, loff_t *pos)
+{
+	struct pen_file *pf = f->private_data;
+	struct gk3_pen *p = pf->p;
+	u8 m[3];
+
+	if (n == sizeof(m)) {
+		if (copy_from_user(m, buf, sizeof(m)))
+			return -EFAULT;
+		if (m[0] == 'B') {
+			pen_bat_set(m);
+			return n;
+		}
+	}
+	mutex_lock(&p->lock);
+	/* after remove the interrupt is gone; don't touch the hardware */
+	if (p->gone) {
+		mutex_unlock(&p->lock);
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
+	p->hints++;
+	p->pen_seen = jiffies;
+	if (p->idle) {
+		p->hint_wakes++;
+		pen_set_idle(p, false);
+	}
+	mutex_unlock(&p->lock);
+	return n;
+}
+
+static __poll_t pen_cdev_poll(struct file *f, poll_table *wait)
+{
+	struct pen_file *pf = f->private_data;
+	struct gk3_pen *p = pf->p;
+
+	poll_wait(f, &p->wq, wait);
+	if (READ_ONCE(p->gone))
+		return EPOLLERR | EPOLLHUP;
+	return READ_ONCE(p->uniq_seq) != pf->last ? EPOLLIN | EPOLLRDNORM : 0;
+}
+
+static const struct file_operations pen_cdev_fops = {
+	.owner = THIS_MODULE,
+	.open = pen_cdev_open,
+	.release = pen_cdev_release,
+	.read = pen_cdev_read,
+	.write = pen_cdev_write,
+	.poll = pen_cdev_poll,
+};
+
+/* ---- driver ---- */
+
+static int gk3_pen_probe(struct spi_device *spi)
+{
+	struct device *dev = &spi->dev;
+	struct gk3_pen *p;
+	int ret;
+
+	/* not devm: open files of /dev/gk3_pen keep it beyond the unbind */
+	p = kzalloc_obj(*p, GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!p)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+	kref_init(&p->ref);
+	ret = devm_add_action_or_reset(dev, pen_put, p);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	p->xfer = devm_kzalloc(dev, HDR_LEN + FRAME_LEN, GFP_KERNEL);
+	p->ring = devm_kcalloc(dev, RING_LEN, sizeof(*p->ring), GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!p->xfer || !p->ring)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+
+	/*
+	 * The panel's follower callbacks stop the watchdog and the idle
+	 * polling while the screen is off.  If the panel has not probed yet the
+	 * follower cannot be added and both would keep running for good, so
+	 * defer until it has, before anything is started.  Other lookup
+	 * failures end in the always-on watchdog below.
+	 */
+	if (drm_is_panel_follower(dev)) {
+		struct device_node *np = of_parse_phandle(dev->of_node, "panel", 0);
+		struct drm_panel *panel = of_drm_find_panel(np);
+
+		of_node_put(np);
+		if (panel == ERR_PTR(-EPROBE_DEFER))
+			return dev_err_probe(dev, -EPROBE_DEFER, "waiting for the panel\n");
+	}
+
+	p->spi = spi;
+	p->tx1_peak_max = S16_MIN;
+	mutex_init(&p->lock);
+	INIT_DELAYED_WORK(&p->idle_poll, pen_idle_poll_fn);
+	init_waitqueue_head(&p->wq);
+	spi_set_drvdata(spi, p);
+
+	spi->mode = spi_mode & 3;
+	spi->bits_per_word = 8;
+	spi->max_speed_hz = speed_hz;
+	ret = spi_setup(spi);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "spi_setup\n");
+
+	p->dbg = debugfs_create_dir("gk3_pen", NULL);
+	debugfs_create_file("stats", 0400, p->dbg, p, &stats_fops);
+	debugfs_create_file("ring", 0400, p->dbg, p, &ring_fops);
+	debugfs_create_file("reinit", 0200, p->dbg, p, &reinit_fops);
+
+	mutex_lock(&p->lock);
+	p->init_ret = pen_hw_init(p, true);
+	mutex_unlock(&p->lock);
+	dev_info(dev, "slave init %d (mode %d, %d Hz, irq %d)\n",
+		 p->init_ret, spi->mode & 3, spi->max_speed_hz, spi->irq);
+
+	mutex_lock(&gk3_pen_dev_lock);
+	gk3_pen_dev = p;
+	mutex_unlock(&gk3_pen_dev_lock);
+	p->misc.minor = MISC_DYNAMIC_MINOR;
+	p->misc.name = "gk3_pen";
+	p->misc.fops = &pen_cdev_fops;
+	p->misc.mode = 0600;
+	ret = misc_register(&p->misc);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_err(dev, "misc_register: %d\n", ret);
+	else
+		p->misc_ok = true;
+
+	/* Stay bound even if the bus check failed: debugfs reinit can retry. */
+	if (!p->init_ret) {
+		ret = pen_start(p);
+		if (ret)
+			dev_err(dev, "start: %d\n", ret);
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * Follow the panel (the DT sets panel = <&panel>).  The enabled
+	 * callback runs right away if the screen is on, which starts the
+	 * watchdog.  Without a panel, run the watchdog unconditionally.
+	 */
+	INIT_DELAYED_WORK(&p->watchdog, pen_watchdog_fn);
+	p->follower.funcs = &pen_follower_funcs;
+	ret = drm_panel_add_follower(dev, &p->follower);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_warn(dev, "no panel to follow (%d), watchdog always on\n", ret);
+		pen_panel_enabled(&p->follower);
+	} else {
+		p->follower_ok = true;
+	}
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static void gk3_pen_remove(struct spi_device *spi)
+{
+	struct gk3_pen *p = spi_get_drvdata(spi);
+
+	/* stop the panel from re-arming the watchdog, then stop the watchdog */
+	if (p->follower_ok)
+		drm_panel_remove_follower(&p->follower);
+	mutex_lock(&p->lock);
+	WRITE_ONCE(p->gone, true);
+	pen_set_idle(p, false);
+	mutex_unlock(&p->lock);
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&p->watchdog);
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&p->idle_poll);
+	wake_up_interruptible(&p->wq);
+	mutex_lock(&gk3_pen_dev_lock);
+	gk3_pen_dev = NULL;
+	mutex_unlock(&gk3_pen_dev_lock);
+	if (p->misc_ok)
+		misc_deregister(&p->misc);
+	if (p->poller)
+		kthread_stop(p->poller);
+	if (use_irq && p->running)
+		devm_free_irq(&spi->dev, spi->irq, p);
+	debugfs_remove_recursive(p->dbg);
+}
+
+static const struct of_device_id gk3_pen_of_match[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "himax,hx83121a-pen-slave" },
+	{ }
+};
+MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, gk3_pen_of_match);
+
+static const struct spi_device_id gk3_pen_ids[] = {
+	{ "hx83121a-pen-slave" },
+	{ }
+};
+MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(spi, gk3_pen_ids);
+
+static struct spi_driver gk3_pen_driver = {
+	.driver = {
+		.name = "himax-hx83121a-pen",
+		.of_match_table = gk3_pen_of_match,
+		/*
+		 * A manual unbind would free the device state while gk3pend
+		 * still has /dev/gk3_pen open.
+		 */
+		.suppress_bind_attrs = true,
+	},
+	.id_table = gk3_pen_ids,
+	.probe = gk3_pen_probe,
+	.remove = gk3_pen_remove,
+};
+
+static int __init gk3_pen_init(void)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	/* not fatal: the pen works without */
+	pen_bat = power_supply_register(NULL, &pen_bat_desc, &pen_bat_cfg);
+	if (IS_ERR(pen_bat)) {
+		pr_warn("battery not registered: %ld\n", PTR_ERR(pen_bat));
+		pen_bat = NULL;
+	}
+
+	ret = spi_register_driver(&gk3_pen_driver);
+	if (ret && pen_bat)
+		power_supply_unregister(pen_bat);
+	return ret;
+}
+
+static void __exit gk3_pen_exit(void)
+{
+	spi_unregister_driver(&gk3_pen_driver);
+	if (pen_bat)
+		power_supply_unregister(pen_bat);
+}
+
+module_init(gk3_pen_init);
+module_exit(gk3_pen_exit);
+
+MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Himax HX83121A cascade slave (active pen) driver for HUAWEI MateBook E Go");
+MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
